From 8fca241f1d4f79030803c1438f1b7184258e710c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tj-barrett <barrett.t@northeastern.edu>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:43:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Check host allocations instead of crashing on out-of-memory

malloc/calloc/realloc results were never checked, and neither were the cudaMallocHost
(pinned) allocations of the L and U factors in MALLOC_HOST nor the cudaMalloc of the
block table. When a factorization did not fit in memory, PaStiX segfaulted later from
many threads at once (e.g. a 1.26M-equation problem in FP64 needs ~56 GB for L+U).

common/pastix_alloc_check.h routes malloc/calloc/realloc to checked wrappers that print
the failed size and location and exit; it is force-included in every C file of the
library, which also covers the PaRSEC task code generated from the .jdf files.
MALLOC_HOST and the block-table cudaMalloc check their CUDA status. Calls through the
refinement solver's malloc function pointer are written (solver.malloc)(n) so that the
function-like macro does not apply to them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
